            <div xml:id="d962">

                <pb facs="0861" n="854" xml:id="pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.94244/194: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-08T16:00:00+09:00">February 8, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 8—7:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Department’s 25, February 6, 3 p.m. I again took up with the Vice Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs orally and informally today the question of smuggling into
                    North China, presenting the facts in general and in detail. Mr. Horinouchi’s
                    comment as formerly was that an improvement in this situation may be expected
                    when Chinese customs tariffs are reduced and it is hoped that the negotiations
                    to this end will soon be resumed.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
